## Narrated sequence (recording-clock timestamps)

| SRT time (approx.) | Evidenced scene |
| --- | --- |
| **00:00–00:01:20** | Narrator explicitly locates cutaway **while the Darkest Delvers are at the kuo-toa village on the All-Bronze Operation**. **Cassius of Atomer and Carrie Underworld** have travelled through the night to **Dungeon Guild Academy** by **Aegis's horse-drawn coach**. Campus is crowded with adventurers, magical gear, familiars and mounts. Cassius confidently threads through the bustle; Carrie struggles to manage loose scrolls and artifacts. They enter **Radiant Lance Theatre**, a large descending circular amphitheatre with benches/tables facing a central stone speaking place. |
| **~00:01:20–00:02:20** | Academy governance: **three ruling finance/board figures** called something like **“Numilari/New Malari”** (working phonetic title) preside from an enclosed box; a heavily armored **majordomo, “Ivorn/Iphorn the Just”**, calls guild masters to the floor. The prior **guildmaster of Keld**, a giant-class guild, asks funds for night patrols against vampires, receives agreement from audience (not necessarily a grant). Cassius's turn is announced, apparently **another** funding request. |
| **~00:02:20–00:04:15** | Cassius formally requests **funds to hire gold-league champions for Atomer OR a gold-league team to clear the Underdark dungeon beneath the city**. Many laugh at the scale of demand. He lists surface incursions: stirges, darkmantles, cranium rats, piercers, gricks, a rust monster and mimic, gelatinous cube, **possible related hook horrors**, and skeletons, shadows, poltergeists and the **flameskull of Withers Keep, now silenced**. Some claims are Cassius's evidence/conjecture, including **possible hook-horror family relationship** and “ancient evil awakening,” not independent GM confirmation. |
| **~00:04:15–00:05:45** | Board member **“Zoltar the Wizened”** (name/title provisional) challenges him to produce proof; Carrie spreads out recovered **horn of blasting, ancient psychic spear shaft(s), and other trophies**, previously entrusted to the guild. A board woman with enormous cats pointedly dismisses her as a mere low-level artificer. Another member (possibly addressed **“Warden/Gigashark”**, speaker/title parsing uncertain) recognizes that **elves left ancient defenses at Underdark entrances**, although this remains the board member's assertion about history. Academy had already funded **two researchers and silver-rank guards** to inspect breached forest ruins nearly **two months earlier**; Cassius complains they have communicated no findings. |
| **~00:05:45–00:07:20** | Cassius explains that his overstretched silver ranks leave **bronze companies doing diplomatic inspections of surrounding ruins** while the city's ordinary ghost/hag jobs continue. Board says special guild-funded work should be uncommon. He invokes Atomer's history as a site of **Proudface's Pelorian temple**, **“Loran's/Loren's final battle”**, a **class-five Oni incursion** and **“the behir of thirty-four”**. These names and events are **Cassius's claims; no independent chronology or identification is established by this monologue**. |
| **~00:07:20–00:08:45** | A board member points to the Delvers as a specially chosen party, apparently selected by **“Tumin Maximus”** (uncertain spelling). Cassius retorts that their success has come alongside recklessness: **Krandal** allegedly profits from healing and hoards spells, **Koh** would risk missions to cure his wife, and **Evelyn** is a schoolgirl looking for love. **These are Cassius's harsh opinions, not objective adjudications or private disclosures to the party**. A white-haired elder with a patterned robe urges patience and says **divination/commune rituals identifying the chosen party are never wrong**—speaker's belief, not objective proof of infallible prophecy. This establishes **senior guild awareness of Koh's wife**, but not how they know, nor that his companions have been told. |
| **~00:08:45–00:09:35** | Board recommends the upcoming **Bronze Ball** as Atomer's financing opportunity, citing the **Withers family's habitual generosity**. Cassius doubts its speed and the family's reliability, warns of places sounding like **“Strongfair/Stormfair”** and **“Temwater”** (unverified phonetics). Ruling figures refuse to treat Atomer as special amid multiple threats. They **deny additional funding**, make a barbed reference to Cassius's **“condition”** (undefined; do not diagnose), and announce **regional director Selenar Everbloom** will inspect the Atomer guild and judge how previous support was used. |
| **~00:09:35–00:10:12** | Next applicant, **“Bubred Hardslayer”** of a **dragon-class guild** whose home is trapped in a **time crystal**, is called; no outcome of that application depicted. Cassius and Carrie depart the theatre. Carrie asks what they will do; Cassius resolves to **return to Atomer** and hope the Darkest Delvers avoid trouble during their absence. They **climb back into Aegis's coach and begin the long return trip**; the cutaway **does not depict their arrival**. |
| **~00:10:12–end** | Host explicitly promises **the final episode of Delvers Season One next week**, followed by a look toward Season Two and guest players. These are **production announcements**, not guild prophecy or fictional acceptance of a new quest. Primary closes **00:10:36.380**; Qwen closes **00:10:58.500** and contains an isolated final “Oh.” Neither difference has been audio-checked. |

## Canon and chronology implications

- **Type/placement:** A real **narrated fictional scene**, not table-play and not a mere retrospective. Research coverage remains archived **S2E00**, but story time is contemporaneous with **S1E10's kuo-toa mission**, **before the S1E12 season finale**. The archive ID is never renumbered. The final “next week” announcement is decisive for placement; the precise calendar date in-world is not established.
- **Cassius and Carrie:** Their absence from the local 8-AM briefing is explained by the academy funding hearing. Cassius **actively advocates major protection** while his direct descriptions of the three Delvers are cynical; the board **refuses gold-rank aid**. Carrie **physically carries/presents** horn and spear trophies before the board, so “never left guild premises with samples” would be false; **no final return or item hand-back shown at S2E00 cutoff**.
- **High-level governance:** Academy theatre, ruling finance board, major-domo, funding scarcity amid vampire threats, previous researcher/silver guards and proposed Selenar inspection **are established as depicted dialogue/action**, but exact rank titles, proper names and historical claims need corroboration. This supplies contextual reason for Selenar's **later appearance in S1E12**, not a newly resolved political plot after the finale.
- **Private information:** Cassius says **Koh is seeking a cure for his wife** before board; this does **not prove Evelyn/Krandal heard or learned of that information**. The divination elder believes in the chosen party; infallibility is **his opinion**. “In your condition” **does not identify a medical state**.
- **Economy:** The guild **denies requested new funding**. Board anticipates financing from a **future Bronze Ball** and mentions previous Withers patronage; **no ball held, donation received or gold-rank champions hired**. Later S1E12 says no special cash reward due northern vampire war; these accounts are compatible.
- **Source conflicts:** `Aegis/Eegis`, `Atomer/Atamer/Atumir`, `Numilari/New Malari`, `Ivorn/Iphorn`, `Tumin Maximus`, `Proudface`, prior-disaster place names, and titles need targeted listening or written-source checks; no mandatory correction by majority vote.

